# Task 15 — Error / 500 Page

**Category:** State & Feedback
**Difficulty:** advanced
**Style school:** Neo-Retro

## The problem

An error page with a friendly visual tone instead of a dry technical
message, softening the experience when something breaks.

## Constraints

- No image of any kind — every visual element is a plain CSS shape.

## Key implementation decisions

- The "sad face" is a single circle (`rounded-full bg-brand-100`) with two
  small rotated squares as eyes and a short, thick bottom-border arc as the
  mouth — all built from `span`/`div` box shapes.
- Avoided combining a Tailwind transform utility (`-translate-x-1/2`) with
  an arbitrary `[transform:...]` value on the same element — both target the
  same `transform` CSS property, and only one would have taken effect
  depending on CSS output order. The mouth uses the utility class alone.
- `flex-1` on the content wrapper centers everything vertically in the
  remaining space below the back link, without needing a fixed height.

